WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.567 line:92%
-You know, obviously we mentioned Texas.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:03.767 line:92%
Texas went through a terrible stretch there

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.934 line:92%
where freezing temperatures, power failures.

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:10.100 line:92%
Some of that was blamed erroneously, it should be noted,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.634 line:92%
on sort of green initiatives.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.801 line:92%
I know you're supportive of those, but you also believe

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:18.934 line:92%
in investing in the climate and green premiums?

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:20.100 line:92%
I hope I'm saying that right.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.868 line:92%
Can you explain that for everyone?

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:27.567 line:92%
-Well, right now a huge range of activities from making

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:31.434 line:92%
cement, to driving your car, to flying on plane

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.934 line:92%
cause these emissions, and it's 51 billion tons.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.767 line:92%
We're going to try to get that down to zero

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.400 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in the next 30 years.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.434 line:92%
That's going to be hard, because right now if you try

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:48.267 line:92%
to do things the green way, it costs a lot more money

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:52.067 line:92%
to make steal or cement without emissions.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.601 line:92%
And so we need a lot of innovation,

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:58.801 line:92%
and so my book says, "Hey, I think we can do this."

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:03.000 line:92%
You know, I've seen innovation solve big problems,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.767 line:92%
and yet we're going to have to really make it a priority

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.634 line:92%
for each year of the next 30 years

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:15.033 line:92%
with a lot of R&amp;D, a lot of good policies.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.934 line:92%
And unless the younger generations is really

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:20.200 line:92%
pushing for it, we probably will miss this,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.567 line:92%
and the world will be a lot less livable.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:27.234 line:92%
-You visited for the book a coal plant, a cement plant,

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:30.501 line:92%
a paper mill, and I was surprised to hear that you were

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.434 line:92%
someone who self-describes yourself

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.734 line:92%
as horrible at chemistry.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.267 line:92%
Has this just always been the case?

00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.467 line:92%
-Yeah, I'm not that dexterous in the lab.

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:43.734 line:92%
I would, you know, spill things, or not get the numbers right.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:46.501 line:92%
You know, when it comes to the theoretical I'm quite good,

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:50.000 line:92%
but I always had to pick a lab partner who was better

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.901 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at hands-on skills,

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.834 line:92%
and that's why I don't do much cooking.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:58.567 line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Probably for the best.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:01.234 line:92%
You know, you've talked about with the vaccine that it was

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:05.167 line:92%
a nice marriage of the private and the public,

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:08.734 line:92%
and despite any invitation -- innovation, excuse me --

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.701 line:92%
that comes from the private sector, the climate will not be

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.767 line:92%
addressed unless people in government

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.667 line:92%
believe it should be addressed.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.634 line:92%
And therefore, on that hand,

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.601 line:92%
you sort of invite people to run for office.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:23.400 line:92%
You think that's really important for those who believe

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.968 line:92%
climate is an issue to find their way into elected office

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:27.701 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and make it a priority.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:33.267 line:92%
Is that one of the ways out of this 30 year plan?

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.734 line:92%
-No, I'm not going to run, but we need

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.667 line:92%
both parties to engage in this.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:41.400 line:92%
They can have different tactics, different ways of getting

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.000 line:92%
the private sector involved, but it's just like, you know,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:49.367 line:92%
we want to avoid war, and so we debate the defense budget,

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.367 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but not that goal.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:56.100 line:92%
And I do see increased interest that, you know,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:00.300 line:92%
if you want to have a moral cause beyond your own success,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.267 line:92%
believing we should make the planet livable

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:07.868 line:92%
and not hurt the poorest, I think that is catching on,

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.567 line:92%
and that's the only reason I think we'll make

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:17.167 line:92%
the investments that could get us to zero by 2050.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.868 line:92%
-Is one of the things that gives you optimism the fact

00:03:19.868 --> 00:03:22.834 line:92%
that the younger generation seems to be taking this more

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:26.000 line:92%
seriously than maybe anyone who's come before?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.167 line:92%
-Yes, and that's got to keep increasing.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:34.334 line:92%
You know, it's got to become something where any politician

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:39.167 line:92%
who's not serious about climate, they're saying that,

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.968 line:92%
"No, that's not what the U.S. is going to stand for,"

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.400 line:92%
that we're going to lead the way,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.200 line:92%
not only in solving the problems,

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.534 line:92%
but building these new industries for green products.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.868 line:92%
-In the end, I do want to leave on a positive note.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:57.901 line:92%
Would you say on the whole, even though you understand

00:03:57.901 --> 00:03:59.634 line:92%
maybe better than anyone what we're up against,

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:02.601 line:92%
are you, on the whole, optimistic?

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.934 line:92%
-Yes. The -- life has improved a lot.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.701 line:92%
The digital revolution's amazing,

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:12.033 line:92%
and we have to apply that American ingenuity, you know?

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:16.667 line:92%
America's still the place where most breakthroughs happen,

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:19.601 line:92%
so we owe it to the world to figure this one out,

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:22.234 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and I think we will.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.634 line:92%
-Well, thank you so much. Congrats on the book.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:27.100 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I hope it sells.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.067 line:92%
Love you to make a little bit of money on this, Bill.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.467 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Definitely need it.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.968 line:92%
"How to Avoid a Climate Disaster: The Solutions We Have

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:36.501 line:92%
and the Breakthroughs We Need" is available now.

